INT. FUNICULAR RAILWAY - CAR 2 - NIGHT

A steep little tram climbing a mountain of lights. Wooden benches, brass rails, windows fogged from breath. Below, the city sprawls like spilled jewelry. The cable hums.

IMANI KARANJA-WELLS (30s, wool coat, camera bag) sits alone on a bench, bundled against the cold. She gazes at the city. A thermos cup warms her hands.

Across the aisle, at the far end, an old couple's empty seats. A conductor's bell hangs unrung. The car climbs, slow and gentle.

At the next stop, the doors hiss open and a MAN steps in, dusting snow from his shoulders: IGNATIUS ABRAMOWITZ (30s, big red scarf, paper bag of roasted chestnuts). He freezes at the sight of her.

IGNATIUS
Imani?

IMANI
Ignatius.

IGNATIUS
I thought you were in Lisbon.

IMANI
I was in Lisbon. Then I wasn't.

IGNATIUS
How long?

IMANI
Three weeks.

He nods. He sits down, one bench across. The doors close. The car climbs on.

IGNATIUS
Chestnut?

IMANI
Sure.

He passes the bag. She takes one. It burns her fingers. She tosses it from hand to hand.

IGNATIUS
They're hot.

IMANI
I noticed.

Silence. The city drops away below the windows.

IGNATIUS
I got your postcard.

IMANI
Did you?

IGNATIUS
Three of them. They all said the same thing.

IMANI
Which was?

IGNATIUS
"Wish you were here."

IMANI
That's the whole message.

IGNATIUS
It's an interesting message to send to a man you left.

She says nothing. She cracks the chestnut. Eats half. Offers him the rest. He takes it.

IMANI
I didn't leave you.

IGNATIUS
You left a note.

IMANI
I left a note because I couldn't say it.

IGNATIUS
Say what?

IMANI
That I was scared.

A light flickers on the car's ceiling. The funicular shudders to a halt. Silence. The cable stops humming.

IGNATIUS
Are we stuck?

IMANI
Looks like it.

A third voice, rough and breathless, cuts in from the platform as the door slides open. A conductor in a gray cap, ENRIQUE VALDÉS-MORROW (60s, whistle around his neck, lantern swinging), leans into the car.

ENRIQUE
Power cut, folks. Ten minutes. Sit tight.

IMANI
Thank you.

IGNATIUS
We're not going anywhere.

Enrique glances from one to the other. He tips his cap and slides the door shut.

IMANI
(quietly)
You said that on purpose.

IGNATIUS
Which part?

IMANI
We're not going anywhere.

He looks at the city. Its lights shimmer through the fogged glass.

IGNATIUS
I meant it.

She leans her head against the window. A tiny smile.

IMANI
Ten minutes.

IGNATIUS
Ten minutes.

IMANI
(very softly)
Then say something.

He opens his mouth. Outside, all the lights in the city flicker, die, and then, one by one, come back.
